    {
      "round": 1,
      "finding": {
        "id": "C-04",
        "reviewer": "review-security-code",
        "severity": "major",
        "file": "src/commands/operator-confirm-review.ts",
        "line": 725,
        "quote": ": `reviewed head: ${facts.head}${headInput === undefined ? \"\" : \" (given by the agent, replaces the recorded head)\"}`,",
        "problem": "The review_complete card accepts a model-supplied head (7-40 hex) that managed.ts uses to replace manifest.target.head before completeHeadGate. The card shows the agent value, not the recorded head, and the digest does not cover the difference.",
        "impact": "Attack vector: an agent (or an injected instruction in the reviewed PR) calls review_complete with head set to the PR's current head SHA after the PR moved past the commit the round actually reviewed. The head gate passes, the manifest records the agent's SHA, and the operator is asked to approve a card whose SHA looks like the current head. The round closes as if it reviewed the latest commit. The brief requires card content (SHA) to come from the package, not from model input; the CLI `--head` is typed by the operator, the card path is typed by the model. Mitigations that keep this from being a blocker: the card does label the value as agent-given, the operator must still press yes, and the gate still demands READY and an evidence level.",
        "suggested_fix": "Preferred: drop `head` from the review_complete input schema and from buildCard/apply, so the card always completes against the head the package recorded; an operator who really needs a different head uses `keryx review complete --head` in a terminal. Alternative: keep the field but show the recorded head next to it on the card (`recorded head: <sha>; the agent asks to replace it with <sha>`), refuse a value that does not prefix-match the recorded head, and fold the recorded head into factsDigest.",
        "evidence": "src/commands/operator-confirm-review.ts:703 declares `head` in the tool input; :679 `head: headInput ?? recorded`; :725 renders the agent value without the recorded one; :753 `...(headInput === undefined ? {} : { head: headInput })` is passed to completeReviewGated. src/review/managed.ts:967-979 replaces `manifest.target.head` with the supplied value and only pushes a warning when it differs from the recorded head; :982 runs completeHeadGate on the replaced manifest. The CLI reaches the same code with an operator-typed --head (src/commands/review.ts runComplete -> completeReviewGated).",
        "confidence": "medium",
        "class_scope": {
          "sites": [
            "src/commands/operator-confirm-review.ts review_complete head parameter (7-40 hex)",
            "src/review/managed.ts completeReviewGated head override before completeHeadGate"
          ],
          "enumeration_method": "keryx ctx rg for completeHeadGate callers (src/review/readiness.ts:337, src/review/managed.ts:982) and for the head parameter in the card spec; only the card path lets a caller-supplied head replace manifest.target.head"
        }
      },
      "claimed_disposition": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "round": 1,
      "finding": {
        "id": "C-40",
        "reviewer": "review-security-code",
        "severity": "info",
        "file": "src/flow/confirm-token.ts",
        "line": 228,
        "quote": "stored.confirmedVia === \"tui-card\" ? \"tui-card-token\" : stored.confirmedVia === \"remote-card\" ? \"remote-card-token\" : \"terminal-token\";",
        "problem": "consumeConfirmationToken builds the SignatureConfirmation without pressedBy/pressedAt although mintConfirmationToken stores them (record gap on the flow-confirm token).",
        "impact": "No attack vector; an audit-completeness gap. A reader of the signature alone sees 'remote-card-token' without who pressed it.",
        "suggested_fix": "If the signature is meant to be self-contained provenance, copy pressedBy/pressedAt into the returned SignatureConfirmation (types.ts already allows them on the confirmation block). Otherwise state in TM-04 that the signature references the token and the token record holds the presser.",
        "evidence": "confirm-token.ts:140 stores pressedBy; confirm-token.ts:215-236 consumeConfirmationToken returns no pressedBy/pressedAt.",
        "confidence": "medium"
      },
      "claimed_disposition": "fixed"
    }
  ],
